				<div class="info">
					<span class="printuser avatarhover"><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/veralta" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(6030962); return false;"  ><img class="small" src="http://www.wikidot.com/avatar.php?userid=6030962&amp;amp;size=small&amp;amp;timestamp=1608366307" alt="Veralta" style="background-image:url(http://www.wikidot.com/userkarma.php?u=6030962)"/></a><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/veralta" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(6030962); return false;" >Veralta</a></span> <span class="odate time_1608302818 format_%25e%20%25b%20%25Y%2C%20%25H%3A%25M%7Cagohover">18 Dec 2020 14:46</span>
														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-4847785">
									

<p>Hello! I can see that you have a somewhat smooth flow of writing in your article, and has a quite concrete view of what you want to convey to the reader. This is already a good sign that you are developing your potential, but as of the moment, I think that you should be more attuned into how people should write SCPs, particularly in terms of clinical tone and the uniqueness of your idea.</p>
<p>Speaking of uniqueness, you can do it by expounding on a single idea from your SCP. For example, you mentioned that it is &quot;8-bit&quot; - why? What is the story behind it? You can do a social commentary on how gamers (hardcore, casual, anything) perceive each other, or reality in general, for example, just by basing off that &quot;8-bit&quot; detail.</p>
<p>You can also tell the story of the Crypt Night Club - it does sound like a good GoI after all. Why are they connected with your 8-bit glasses? There's potential here, and I am somewhat interested in it.</p>
<p>In short, you should focus on polishing your clinical tone, your idea (once again, focus on one thing), and have a good story or narrative in mind. &quot;Perception defines reality&quot; - how can this be uniquely written considering that you have things like &quot;8-bit&quot; and the night club?</p>
<p>Good luck, and have a good time writing again for this site :)</p>

							</div>

								
					
